      "title": "Read me",
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653",
      "widgets_values": [
        "## Style transfer with FLUX.2\n\n**input_image** \u2014 the picture whose composition you keep.\n**input_image_2** \u2014 the picture you take the look from.\n\nSocket order matters. The prompt says \"the first image\" and \"the second image\", so swapping the two Load Image nodes reverses the effect.\n\n`disable_pup` is **on**. FLUX.2 [pro] rewrites prompts by default and that rewrite tends to soften a precise instruction like this one. Turn it off if you would rather it embellish.\n\n`width` / `height` are **0** \u2014 match the input image. Any other value must be at least 64.\n\nConnect a third reference and a fourth socket appears, up to 8.\n\n### Prompt shape that works\n> Redraw the first image in the style of the second. Keep *(what stays)*. Take only *(what transfers)*.\n\nNaming what must **not** change is what keeps the subject intact."
      ]
    },
